    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate`) is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nTwo changes, chosen to keep structural impact minimal \u2014 **zero existing functions modified**:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). The generator produces the DTO accessors.\n\n2. **New `OwnerPossibleDuplicateAdvice.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained `ResponseBodyAdvice`, modeled directly on the existing `OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice`. For any `OwnerDto` being returned, it finds the earliest existing owner (lower id) that shares the last name (case-insensitive) and postcode but has a different normalized telephone, then sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` accordingly.\n\n### Why this design\n\n- The soft-match flag must survive a later `GET /owners/{id}` (the test reads it back that way), and it must be a *creation-time* fact \u2014 only the earlier owner (`other.getId() < owner.getId()`) counts, so the pre-existing owner is flagged, not the original. Computing this at response time from `findAllOwners()` mirrors how `bulkSignupWarning` already works and avoids any model/schema/mapper churn.\n- \"Not a hard duplicate\" is automatically satisfied: a whole-`identityKey` match is rejected with 409 before creation, and a differing telephone always yields a different key.\n- Telephone comparison reuses the existing `OwnerIdentityKey.telephone(...)` normalization so it agrees with the hard-duplicate rule.\n- MapStruct isn't touched \u2014 the new DTO fields aren't populated from the entity, only by the advice.\n\nNo existing method changed, no class grew, and the one new class carries little surrounding complexity.",
